cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "eproc: Sub-microsecond anytime-valid online statistical inference, multi-rate conformal calibration, and Byzantine-safe multi-agent fusion"
message: "If you use eproc in research, benchmarks, or production evaluation pipelines, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-22"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/pgg898200-ship-it/eproc"
url: "https://pgg898200-ship-it.github.io/eproc/"
authors:
  - name: "eproc contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/pgg898200-ship-it/eproc"
abstract: >-
  eproc is a zero-allocation C11/SIMD and zero-dependency Python statistical
  inference engine providing anytime-valid ONS betting e-processes, O(1)
  Empirical-Bernstein and Normal-Mixture confidence sequences, multi-arm agent
  racing, multi-rate crossing-free AgACI + Conformal PID online calibration,
  fixed 640-byte abelian conformal monoids for distributed leave-one-out fleet
  calibration, Byzantine-safe multi-agent fusion with lock-free seqlocked
  weights, provenance-deduplicated belief pooling, causal Horvitz-Thompson
  subsampling, and an MCP 2026-07-28 stdio server.
keywords:
  - e-process
  - anytime-valid
  - confidence-sequence
  - conformal-prediction
  - sequential-testing
  - multi-agent
  - byzantine-fault-tolerance
  - horvitz-thompson
  - mcp-server
  - c11
